            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "HUGMEHUGS"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I have been eating tomato sandwiches for many years. I tried this mayo/ketchup combo and it just didn't work for me. I will stick with plain mayo. I often will put sliced cucumber on the sandwich too. Doubly good!!",
            "datePublished": "2011-06-27T18:06:27.437Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Pati Carter-Nielsen"
            },
            "reviewBody": "It's also called a \"sink sandwich\" because you eat it standing over the sink so the juice form the tomatoes can run down your arm and into the sink. :-) we eat them all summer with beefsteak tomatoes from our garden. Tastes great with just mayo too.",
            "datePublished": "2013-01-15T11:24:02.017Z"
          },
